BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dead Lover
DTSTART:20250524T065900Z
DTEND:20250524T083400Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T065900Z
UID:xMRwlFy0kJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 82 mins (1h22m)\n\nGrace Glowicki (Tito\, SIFF 2021
 ’s Strawberry Mansion) writes\, directs\, and gives a barkingly daring l
 ead performance in this bizarre\, performance art-coded\, gender-bending l
 o-fi Frankenstein comedy about a lonely gravedigger who will do anything t
 o build the perfect man. SXSW NEON Auteur Award winner. Get in the right h
 eadspace for this absolute ride of a film with a trivia giveaway hosted by
  BoneBat Comedy of Horrors Film Fest before the May 23 screening. Go even 
 deeper into the satire and weird vibes at the May 24 screening with a tick
 et giveaway to Annex Theatre’s upcoming production of "Alice in Arabiala
 nd."\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/dead-lover\n\nAlso playing at:\n  
 • AMC Pacific Place 11 (Sat 24 May\, 1:45 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Souleymane’s Story
DTSTART:20250524T190000Z
DTEND:20250524T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T190000Z
UID:EbgxpYqjJY
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 92 mins (1h32m)\n\nGuinean immigrant Souleymane has 
 applied for asylum in France. Soon he’ll have an interview with the gove
 rnment agency that will change his life…if only he can figure out the ri
 ght story to tell. This film is generously sponsored by Mike Weidemann in 
 memory of Tove Lund and Bruce Hawley. Also sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/festival/souleymanes-story\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Diamonds
DTSTART:20250524T213000Z
DTEND:20250524T235500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T213000Z
UID:pS7ocdFUbB
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 135 mins (2h15m)\n\nIn this lush\, metatheatrical cr
 owdpleaser that was a box office smash in its native Italy\, SIFF favorite
  Ferzan Özpetek gathers 18 of his country’s greatest actresses to tell 
 the story of a Rome-based tailoring shop that makes costumes for the big s
 creen. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/diamonds\n\nAlso pla
 ying at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Sun 25 May\, 7:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2025 Closing Night Film & Party
DTSTART:20250525T010000Z
DTEND:20250525T031000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T010000Z
UID:fKif6hQ1cd
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nEva Victor (“Billions”) writ
 es\, directs\, and stars in this nonlinear\, seriocomic story about a mela
 ncholic English professor’s complicated path toward healing in the after
 math of an all-too-common tragedy. Winner of the Sundance 2025 Waldo Salt 
 Screenwriting Award.  Director\, writer\, and star Eva Victor scheduled t
 o attend. Closing Night Film & Party Tickets: $78 Members | $88 Non-Member
 s Members: Make sure to sign in to your SIFF account before selecting tick
 ets. Note: SIFF parties are for ages 21+\, and IDs will be checked at the 
 door. No refunds will be issued for tickets purchased with an invalid ID.\
 n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/sorry-baby
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Waves
DTSTART:20250525T040000Z
DTEND:20250525T062500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T040000Z
UID:nNaQrMKhLH
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 131 mins (2h11m)\n\nIt’s 1967 Czechoslovakia\, and
  technician Tomás has just started working at the country’s most renown
 ed radio station. But as the Soviets crack down on any dissenting opinions
 \, Tomás must either become an informant or protect his activist younger 
 brother in this nerve-wracking journalism thriller. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps
 ://www.siff.net/festival/waves\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scarecrow in a Garden of Cucumbers
DTSTART:20250525T065900Z
DTEND:20250525T083400Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T065900Z
UID:S05r0VOUQu
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 82 mins (1h22m)\n\nIn this camp classic from 1972 bu
 rsting with lo-fi queer cinema energy\, Warhol Factory muse and trans actr
 ess Holly Woodlawn stars as a small-town girl hoping to make it big in New
  York City. This long-thought-lost treasure is newly restored by the Acade
 my Film Archive. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/scarecrow-
 in-a-garden-of-cucumbers
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
